vation='read', impl_source='oh_aci'), **FileEditAction**\nPath: [/etc/cron.d/tmp-cleanup]\nThought: I will create an hourly cron job that safely removes only regular files and empty directories in /tmp older than 7 days, and logs deletions. Reasoning and constraints:\n- Treat the supplied task path as absolute and operate within the repo environment.\n- Be conservative to avoid removing sockets, active files or non-empty directories: only delete regular files (-type f) and empty directories (-type d -empty) older than 7 days.\n- Use /etc/cron.d so the schedule runs hourly as root without needing an executable bit on a script file.\n- Log deletions to /var/log/tmp-cleanup.log. Note: this assumes the environment has cron enabled and allows writing to /etc/cron.d and /var/log; if not, I will report back.\nCommand: create\nCreated File with Text:\n```\n# /etc/cron.d/tmp-cleanup\n# Hourly cleanup of /tmp: remove regular files and empty directories older than 7 days.\n# Runs as root. Adjust mtime (+7) if you want a different retention window.\nSHELL=/bin/sh\nPATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/sbin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin\n\n# Minute Hour Day Month DayOfWeek User Command\n# This runs at minute 0 of every hour.\n0 * * * * root /bin/sh -c 'find /tmp -mindepth 1 -type f -mtime +7 -print -delete; find /tmp -mindepth 1 -type d -empty -mtime +7 -print -delete' >> /var/log/tmp-cleanup.log 2>&1\n```\n, FileEditObservation(content='File created successfully at: /etc/cron.d/tmp-cleanup', path='/etc/cron.d/tmp-cleanup', prev_exist=False, old_content=None, new_content=None, observation='edit', impl_source='oh_aci', diff=\"--- /etc/cron.d/tmp-cleanup\\n+++ /etc/cron.d/tmp-cleanup\\n@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@\\n+# /etc/cron.d/tmp-cleanup\\n+# Hourly cleanup of /tmp: remove regular files and empty directories older than 7 days.\\n+# Runs as root. Adjust mtime (+7) if you want a different retention window.\\n+SHELL=/bin/sh\\n+PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/sbin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin\\n@@ -